.TH EXIT-OPTIONS 1 "August 2026" "exit-options" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
exit-options \- pop-up dialog with system exit options for MX Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B exit-options
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B exit-options
displays a pop-up dialog offering system exit options such as lock,
logout, suspend, reboot and shutdown. It is designed for use with MX
Linux desktop environments, in particular Fluxbox, IceWM and JWM.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-vertical\fR
Display the buttons in a vertical window.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-horizontal\fR
Display the buttons in a horizontal window.
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-timeout\fR \fIseconds\fR
Timeout duration in seconds. Use \fIoff\fR to disable the timeout.
.TP
\fB\-\-help\fR
Display help about the available options and exit.
.PP
The display orientation option used will be remembered and used the
next time the application is started.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings may also be set in
.I ~/.config/MX-Linux/exit-options.conf
(user configuration) or
.I /etc/exit-options.conf
(system\-wide configuration), which is read if no user configuration
exists. Command line options take precedence over configuration file
settings.
.PP
Recognized configuration keys include:
.TP
.B layout
Set to \fIhorizontal\fR or \fIvertical\fR.
.TP
.B timeout
Timeout in seconds, or \fIoff\fR to disable it.
.TP
.B LockIcon, LogoutIcon, SuspendIcon, RebootIcon, ShutdownIcon
Path to a custom icon file to use for the given action.
.TP
.B IconSize, Margin, Spacing
Layout tuning options for the button icons.
.SH FILES
.I ~/.config/MX-Linux/exit-options.conf
.br
.I /etc/exit-options.conf
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fluxbox (1)
